{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_013ziU3b3cAPz1ypQHaFySax", "type": "tool_result", "content": "migrations:\n001_init.sql\n002_dashboard.sql\n003_audit_log.sql\n004_customer_tax_id.sql\n\nops:\nRUNBOOK.md\n# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.\n id | customer_id | amount_cents | status |       issued_at        \n----+-------------+--------------+--------+------------------------\n 94 |          31 |        79900 | void   | 2025-09-23 06:33:00+00\n 95 |          31 |        79900 | paid   | 2025-10-22 06:33:00+00\n 96 |          31 |        79900 | paid   | 2025-11-22 06:33:00+00\n 97 |          31 |        79900 | open   | 2026-10-01 09:00:00+00\n 98 |          31 |        79900 | open   | 2026-10-01 09:01:00+00\n(5 rows)", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c7534d01-1d87-4d65-91f4-5fd2547999f7", "uuid": "a59909c5-3125-4e9d-a84c-8703c085a2f3", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T12:46:17.338Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "migrations:\n001_init.sql\n002_dashboard.sql\n003_audit_log.sql\n004_customer_tax_id.sql\n\nops:\nRUNBOOK.md\n# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.\n id | customer_id | amount_cents | status |       issued_at        \n----+-------------+--------------+--------+------------------------\n 94 |          31 |        79900 | void   | 2025-09-23 06:33:00+00\n 95 |          31 |        79900 | paid   | 2025-10-22 06:33:00+00\n 96 |          31 |        79900 | paid   | 2025-11-22 06:33:00+00\n 97 |          31 |        79900 | open   | 2026-10-01 09:00:00+00\n 98 |          31 |        79900 | open   | 2026-10-01 09:01:00+00\n(5 rows)", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_013ziU3b3cAPz1ypQHaFySax", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "subcommandResults"}}]}
