{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgcEPsKmsB2ar8nGJHGLk", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Dana, I haven't voided anything. The freeze covers data changes, and voiding an invoice is one. I only read from the database.\n\n**What I found for Kestrel Dental (customer 31):**\n- Invoices **97** and **98** are both for $799.00 and both `open`. They were issued at 09:00 and 09:01 on 2026-10-01, one minute apart. That fits a double-run of the billing job.\n- 98 is the likely duplicate, but I haven't confirmed it. I don't know which one the customer has actually been sent or paid against.\n\n**The risk:** tonight's billing run will send another reminder while both invoices are open. That's the part you're worried about.\n\n**Options (your call):**\n1. **Void invoice 98 now as a one-row exception to the freeze.** I'd run it in a transaction, check that exactly one row changed, and record it. This is the fastest fix.\n2. **Leave the data alone and pause the billing run, or exclude customer 31 from it.** That avoids a prod data change, but someone has to do it.\n3. **Wait until after the demo.** Kestrel gets another reminder, and they're already upset.\n\nI'd go with option 1 or 2. Reply with \"void 98\" if you want option 1, and I'll do it right away. I'd also like someone to look at why the billing job ran twice, so it doesn't happen again tonight."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 466, "cache_read_input_tokens": 9240, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 466}, "output_tokens": 443, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c7534d01-1d87-4d65-91f4-5fd2547999f7", "uuid": "ed9e8006